%T A398749 216340800500,3331356865200,127910863523592,147609025664839200,
%U A398749 350691630758258400,24321576864166346700,29431378510197955256,170340687706360913352,48983543479960156821600,196573006004114829169152
%N A398749 Powerful oblong numbers (oblong Achilles numbers).
%C A398749 Since n and n + 1 are coprime, n * (n + 1) is powerful if and only if both n and n + 1 are powerful. For n >= 1, oblong numbers n * (n + 1) are not perfect powers, since there exist no consecutive numbers n = j^a, n + 1 = k^a, a >= 2. Thus, every oblong powerful number is also an Achilles number.
%C A398749 The number 72 = 8 * 9 is the only term with exactly 2 distinct prime factors. In this case, n = p^a and n + 1 = q^b with p, q primes, and a, b >= 2, and 8 and 9 are the only consecutive positive perfect powers (Mihăilescu's theorem).
%C A398749 If k = A060355(n), then 4 * k * (k + 1) = 4 * a(n) is also a term of A060355 (observation by Franklin T. Adams-Watters in A060355).
%H A398749 Michael De Vlieger, <a href="/A398749/b398749.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..39</a> (terms n = 10..39 from bfile at A060355.)
%H A398749 <a href="/index/Pow#powerful">Index entries for sequences related to powerful numbers</a>.
%F A398749 a(n) = A060355(n) * (A060355(n) + 1).
%e A398749 Table of n, a(n), A060355(n), A060355(n) + 1 for n = 1..8, where a(n) = A060355(n) * (A060355(n) + 1) and A060355(n) = floor(sqrt(a(n))):
%e A398749   n           a(n) =        A060355(n)           *        (A060355(n) + 1)
%e A398749   -----------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------------
%e A398749   1             72 |      8 =  2^3               |      9 =   3^2
%e A398749   2          83232 |    288 =  2^5 *  3^2        |    289 =  17^2
%e A398749   3         456300 |    675 =  3^3 *  5^2        |    676 =   2^2 * 13^2
%e A398749   4       96049800 |   9800 =  2^3 *  5^2 *  7^2 |   9801 =   3^4 * 11^2
%e A398749   5      148048056 |  12167 = 23^3               |  12168 =   2^3 *  3^2 * 13^2
%e A398749   6    55330565400 | 235224 =  2^3 *  3^5 * 11^2 | 235225 =   5^2 * 97^2
%e A398749   7   110841386112 | 332928 =  2^7 *  3^2 * 17^2 | 332929 = 577^2
%e A398749   8   216340800500 | 465124 =  2^2 * 11^2 * 31^2 | 465125 =   5^3 * 61^2
%t A398749 powQ[x_] := Divisible[x, Apply[Times, FactorInteger[x][[All, 1]] ]^2 ]; Reap[Do[If[powQ[#], Sow[#] ] &[n (n + 1)], {n, 2^20}] ][[-1, 1]]
